## Adding CVAR Variables

When adding a new cvar (console variable), it must be added to **the end** of the following lists:

1. **In main file** (e.g., `cg_main.c`): Add the `vmCvar_t` variable declaration at the end of the variable declarations list (before `static cvarTable_t cvarTable[]`)
2. **In cvarTable array**: Add the entry at the end of `static cvarTable_t cvarTable[]` array
3. **In local header** (e.g., `cg_local.h`): Add the `extern vmCvar_t` declaration at the end of the extern declarations list

**Important**: 
- New cvars are always added at the **bottom/end** of each list, never in the middle.
- **Always add the `CVAR_NEW` flag** to new cvar entries in the `cvarTable[]` array (e.g., `CVAR_ARCHIVE | CVAR_NEW`).
- **Always add descriptions** for new cvars. See detailed rules in `@OSP2-PBE/.cursor/rules/Description rules`:
  - Add descriptions in `assets/OSP2.cfg` (Russian) and `assets/OSP2English.cfg` (English) after `/belist` command
  - Add descriptions in `code/cgame/cg_cvardescriptions.c` in `cvarDescriptionTable[]` array at the end
  - Descriptions should be added when work is completed

Example:
```c
// In cg_main.c - add at end of vmCvar_t declarations
vmCvar_t        cg_simpleItemsBob;
vmCvar_t        cg_newCvar;  // ✓ Add new cvar here at the end

// In cvarTable[] - add at end of array
static cvarTable_t cvarTable[] =
{
    // ... existing entries ...
    { &cg_simpleItemsBob, "cg_simpleItemsBob", "0", CVAR_ARCHIVE },
    { &cg_newCvar, "cg_newCvar", "0", CVAR_ARCHIVE | CVAR_NEW },  // ✓ Add new entry here at the end
};

// In cg_local.h - add at end of extern declarations
extern vmCvar_t           cg_simpleItemsBob;
extern vmCvar_t           cg_newCvar;  // ✓ Add new extern here at the end
```
